# A generic service definition that transmits a single signed integer value in the request,
# and returns a boolean indicating success or failure.
#
# This service is intended for use in systems where a discrete value—such as an ID, count,
# or command index—is transmitted with metadata and acknowledged after processing.
#
# The header allows this service request to be synchronized with other data sources in time and space,
# while the `data` field carries the core value being acted on, and the `success` response confirms
# whether the request was successfully handled.

std_msgs/Header header
int32 data
---
bool success
